# Mend Landing Page — Project Rules

## What this is
A single-page waitlist landing site for **Mend**: automated design QA for AI-built apps.
Mend crawls a live app, finds UI/UX issues, lets you review them (table or card view), and helps you ship complete.
Primary audience: **product designers**. Secondary: startup founders.
Domain: **mendit.net**. One page, anchor-linked sections. No routing library.

The design is **already finished in Figma**. Your job is to implement it faithfully, not to redesign it.
This is a design-QA product: the page itself is the proof of craft. Pixel accuracy, alignment, spacing consistency, and motion quality are the product pitch.

## Stack (do not add to this without asking)
- Vite + React 19 + TypeScript (strict)
- Tailwind CSS v4 via `@tailwindcss/vite` (CSS-first config with `@theme` in `src/index.css`; no `tailwind.config.js` unless needed)
- `motion` (Framer Motion) — import from `"motion/react"` — for web-native motion only
- `lottie-react` — for vector animations exported from After Effects (Bodymovin)
- Native `<video>` — for raster/PNG animations exported as MP4 (+ WebM when available)
- `@supabase/supabase-js` — waitlist RPC only
- `posthog-js` + `@vercel/analytics` — analytics
- No UI component library. No CSS-in-JS. No state library. No router.

