## Design system

### Source of truth
1. **Figma (via MCP)** for layout, spacing, sizes, radii, colors, type.
2. **This file** for copy and behavior.
Never invent values. If a value is missing from Figma, ask — do not guess.

### Tokens
Pull exact values with the Figma MCP (`get_variable_defs` on the frame) and define them once in `src/index.css` under `@theme`. Use only tokens in components — **no raw hex values or arbitrary pixel values in JSX** unless Figma has a one-off and you comment why.

Token names to use (fill values from Figma):
```css
@theme {
  /* surfaces */
  --color-bg:            /* page background (near-black) */;
  --color-surface:       /* cards/panels: dark charcoal, one step lifted off bg */;
  --color-surface-2:     /* nested/raised surface */;
  --color-border:        /* hairline borders on surfaces */;
  --color-frame:         /* blue section containers behind product visuals */;

  /* text */
  --color-text:          /* primary text */;
  --color-text-muted:    /* secondary text */;
  --color-text-accent:   /* muted blue-grey used in "found and fixed." */;

  /* state colors — RESERVED for issues and fixes only */
  --color-issue:         /* red: problems, low score */;
  --color-fixed:         /* green: resolved, high score, checkmarks */;
  --color-warn:          /* amber issue tags */;

  /* type */
  --font-sans:           /* from Figma */;

  /* radii, from Figma */
  --radius-pill:  9999px;
  --radius-card:  /* from Figma */;
  --radius-frame: /* from Figma */;
}
```

### Rules
- **Dark cohesion:** every card and panel uses the same surface color, border treatment, and radius family. No colored card backgrounds.
- **Color is reserved for fixes and issues.** Red/green/amber appear only on issue states, fix states, scores, and tags. Never as decoration.
- The email field is a **pill with the button inside it** (hero, Mendboards, final CTA share one `EmailCapture` component with variants).
- Sentence case everywhere except the locked strings above.
- No gradient washes, no glow blobs, no decorative shadows, no extra eyebrows/labels that aren't in Figma.
- Body line length ≤ ~70ch.

### Quality floor (non-negotiable)
- Responsive: test at 375, 768, 1280, 1440, 1920. Desktop is the design target; laptop (1280–1440) must look intentional, not squeezed.
- Visible keyboard focus on every interactive element (`focus-visible` ring using a token).
- `prefers-reduced-motion`: all animations resolve to their **final (fixed) state** as a still.
- Semantic HTML: one `<h1>` (hero headline), `<section>` with `aria-labelledby`, `<nav>`, `<footer>`.
- Images: explicit `width`/`height`, `loading="lazy"` below the fold, WebP where possible.
- Lighthouse: aim for 95+ performance and 100 accessibility.

## Motion

### Division of labor
| Kind | Tool | Used for |
|---|---|---|
| Vector component animations | Lottie (`LottieSlot`) | Hero components (button, avatar, user card, payment screen, toggle, chart card), Scan panel, pins |
| Raster/screen animations | MP4 (`VideoSlot`) | Scan / Audit / Ship screen loops, anything with photos or blur |
| Web-native interaction | `motion/react` | Nav, Figma-vs-Build slider, button press feedback, the hero highlight sequencer |

The animations are **not built yet**. Build every slot so the asset can be dropped in later without touching layout:
- Each slot has a fixed aspect ratio matching the Figma frame (no layout shift when the asset loads).
- Until an asset exists, render the static Figma export (PNG/WebP) of the **broken** state as a placeholder, with a `// TODO(motion): <name>` comment.

### `LottieSlot`
- Props: `animationData`, `playOnView` (default true), `loop` (default false), `onComplete`, `ariaLabel`.
- Plays **once** when ≥40% in view, then **rests on the final frame**. Never visibly snaps back to the broken state.
- Exposes an imperative `play()` (via ref) so a sequencer can trigger it.
- Reduced motion: jump to last frame, no playback.

### `VideoSlot`
- `<video muted playsInline preload="metadata" poster=…>` with MP4 (+ WebM source if present).
- Plays when in view, pauses when out of view. Loops only if the clip's reset is hidden inside a fade (asset responsibility); otherwise plays once and rests.
- Reduced motion: show the **final-frame poster**, no playback.

### Hero sequencer (spec — build the scaffold now)
- Components are scattered around the centered headline; the headline is the centerpiece.
- Sequence: highlight one component at a time (others dim to ~45% opacity), local Mend cursor blips in on it, click-dip, fixes fire ~100ms after the dip, cursor fades, next component highlights. Cross-fade handoffs.
- Fixes **stay fixed**. Play once on load/view; rest on the fully fixed state.
- Keep total sequence under ~10s. Small components (button, toggle) ~600–800ms; user card ~2.3s cascade.
- Implementation: each component is its own `LottieSlot`; the cursor is an HTML element animated with `motion/react`; the sequencer calls each slot's `play()` on cursor arrival.

### Motion quality rules
- Never linear easing. Default ease: `[0.22, 1, 0.36, 1]`; snaps use a spring with slight overshoot (`type: "spring", stiffness: 400, damping: 28`).
- Overshoot-and-settle on every fix. Stagger multi-part changes 100–300ms.
- No scroll-triggered fade-and-slide-up on every section. Motion is spent on the product visuals, not on generic entrances.

### Figma vs Build slider
- Real component, not a video. Two stacked images (design left, build right) clipped by a draggable divider.
- Pointer + touch drag, and keyboard: the handle is `role="slider"` with `aria-valuenow`, arrow keys move 5%, Home/End to edges.
- Starts at 50%. Optional one-time nudge animation on first view to show it's draggable (skipped under reduced motion).

### Mendboards banner
- Dotted grid background + occasional shooting stars. Implement in CSS (or a tiny canvas) — keep it subtle and cheap; pause when off-screen; static under reduced motion.

## Waitlist & analytics
- Supabase only via RPC `join_waitlist` — never query waitlist tables directly from the client.
- `src/lib/supabase.ts` builds a single client from `VITE_SUPABASE_URL` + `VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` (null + warning if missing).
- `joinWaitlist({ email, list, source })` in `src/lib/waitlist.ts`:
  - `list`: `"main" | "mendboards"`
  - `source`: `"hero" | "mendboards" | "final-cta"`
  - Trims/lowercases email; returns `invalid_email` without calling the server when invalid.
  - Sends UTM (`utm_source` / `utm_medium` / `utm_campaign`) captured on first load (module cache + `sessionStorage`) and `document.referrer`.
  - `"already"` is success. Dev stub (~600ms) when Supabase env is missing.
- Joined-state keys in `localStorage`: `mend:joined:main`, `mend:joined:mendboards` (`src/lib/joined.ts` + `useJoined`). Hero + final CTA share `main`; Mendboards is independent.
- Ticket success UI: `TicketModal` — copy lives in `copy.ts` under `ticket` / `emailCapture`.
- Analytics (`src/lib/analytics.ts`): PostHog via `track(event, props)` only. Events: `section_viewed`, `waitlist_field_focused`, `waitlist_submitted`, `waitlist_joined`, `waitlist_error`, `ticket_shared`, `nav_clicked`, `slider_dragged`. Vercel `<Analytics />` in `App`. No-op when keys are missing. Never identify by email.

